<title>GERMANY: EU soybean crush 13 percent higher in January.</title>
<headline>EU soybean crush 13 percent higher in January.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>January soybean crushings in the European Union of 1.45 million tonnes were 13 percent up from a year earlier, the independent Oil World newsletter said.</p>
<p>The publication cited a faster rate of processing in Germany, the Benelux countries, Britain, France and Italy.</p>
<p>January sunseed crushings totalled 550,00 tonnes, up from 470,000 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Rapeseed processing, at 560,000 tonnes, was well below the 750,000 tonnes seen a year earlier, but above earlier expectations as Germany, the Benelux countries and Britain handled higher volumes.</p>
<p>The combined crush of the three oilseeds in January was 2.56 million tonnes, up from 2.50 million in January 1996.</p>
<p>But cumulative Sept/Jan 96/97 crushings, at 12.02 million, were slightly below 12.03 million processed in Sept/Jan 95/96.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
